// Title: Non-privileged Usage of Reg or Powershell
// ID: 8f02c935-effe-45b3-8fc9-ef8696a9e41d
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Teymur Kheirkhabarov (idea), Ryan Plas (rule), oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-05
// Tags: attack.persistence, attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1112
// Description: Search for usage of reg or Powershell by non-privileged users to modify service configuration in registry
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "reg " AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS "add")) OR ((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "powershell" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS "set-itemproperty" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS " sp " OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS "new-itemproperty"))) AND ((IntegrityLevel = "Medium" OR IntegrityLevel = "S-1-16-8192") AND (src.process.cmdline containsCIS "ControlSet" AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS "Services") AND (src.process.cmdline containsCIS "ImagePath" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS "FailureCommand" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS "ServiceDLL")))
